## Catalog graph (data)

The focused set is a `CatalogGraph`. Nodes are `card` (catalog id) and `phrase` (one normalized key for chips, deck pins, harvest, and `reviewFeed`). Helpers and keywords are phrases. Attaching a theme **pins a phrase**; it is not a stored type.

Incidence edges are **native oracle**, not Theme lanes: card → phrase as `trigger` | `condition` | `effect` | `type` | `keyword` (`cost` when flatten stops dropping it). Harvest: phrase → phrase as `produce` | `count`. Warm: card → card as `pair` when community exists. `kind` lives on the edge.

Wants / Needs / Is / Says is Theme **chrome** — an insight map over incidence. Do not store `says` on the graph (that collapses keyword-Says with leftover-effect Says). Lock-set is a query: `trigger` ∪ `condition` ∪ `effect`. Not `type`. Not `keyword`. Multicolor is presence of a lock card with two or more colors, not a gold census.

Build per focused set on the client. Do not compile at ingest.

## Passes and cuts (logic)

Writers are `(graph, corpus) => graph` in `passes/`. Readers are insight cuts. Components do not harvest.

Sibling modules, layered in time:

- **Layer 0** — parse / diction / corpus. POS/frame tagging (verb `counter` vs noun `counter`) belongs here, before first-order mint. Glue-delete is the same slot. Not this rewrite.
- **Layer 1** — mint chips via concentration as today; link incidence and harvest from printed frames. "The Ring tempts you appears on 51 cards" is incidence degree, not an NLP input.
- **Layer 2** — phrase proximity from graph neighborhood. Not this rewrite.
- **Layer 3** — `warm-pair`. Same pass contract; empty until `SetCommunity` is in hand. Do not block the graph on the network. Warm **links**, it does not mint chips.

Two harvest shapes. **Produce:** the mechanic supplies a named object (Amass → Army; Ring `is legendary`). **Count:** `for each X` in the reminder means X enables the printed phrase (`human` feeds `affinity for humans`), not the reverse. `for each` is glue in concentration, not a theme chip. Do not fold it into `GLUE_PHRASES`.

Do not derive rules consequences from a filter (The Battle of Bywater “spares” power &lt; 3). That relation is warm. Cold names Food and the printed scaler. Paraphrase NLP (health ≈ life) is not a layer.

Keywords are chips from `keywords[]` plus oracle, not a per-set list. Join text from same-line reminder, companion faces, and helper oracle.

Copy-peak and land color-fix are deck-health, not `pair` kinds. Provenance stays on the edge (`pair` vs `produce`).

## Discovery cuts (UI parity)

Same product, new owners. Set board: chips ranked by **concentration** (default, scoped count) or **emergence** (lift); sort only; show the number for the active knob; drag a chip onto a deck to pin. Library: equal grid. Theme: inspect one selected phrase as Wants/Needs/Is/Says. Suggestions: neighbors of the pinned set (`produce`, `count`, `pair`); feed click jumps to Theme. Do not merge the tabs in this rewrite.
